selec 1 -> near "selec": syntax error
select 1; select 2 -> One statement per `sql(...)`: split it into one call per statement.
select :a -> Parameters are `?`, taken from the list in order; named and numbered parameters are a second spelling.
select random() -> `random()` reads randomness: compute the value in vo (std.random) and pass it as a parameter.
select datetime('now') -> `'now'` reads the clock: compute the time in vo (std.time) and pass it as a parameter.
pragma journal_mode = wal -> PRAGMA journal_mode = WAL is not available in vo
select * from no_such_table -> run: error: no such table: no_such_table
select ? + 1 -> 1 row(s)
